// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`init project-instructions prompt matches the scaffold prompt snapshot 1`] = `
"Generate a file named AGENTS.md at the root of this project that serves as a contributor guide for both humans and coding agents.

First inspect the repository to ground every statement in what is actually here: read the existing project files, the build system and package manifests, the test setup, any README or docs, and existing guidance files (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README). Do not invent commands, conventions, or structure that you cannot verify in the repo.

Before writing, check whether AGENTS.md already exists at the project root. If it does, do NOT overwrite or replace it — read it, preserve the useful existing instructions, and offer to append or improve it in place instead. Only create a new file when none exists.

Title the document "Repository Guidelines". Follow the outline below, but adapt as needed — add sections if relevant, and omit those that do not apply to this project:

- Project Structure & Module Organization
- Build, Test, and Development Commands (with a one-line description of what each command does)
- Coding Style & Naming Conventions
- Testing Guidelines
- Commit & Pull Request Guidelines
- Security & Configuration Tips (only if relevant)

Use Markdown headings (#, ##) for structure. Keep the document concise: 200-400 words is optimal. Keep explanations short, direct, and specific to this repository, and maintain a professional, instructional tone. Write the file through your normal file-writing tool so it goes through the usual approval, and keep the change scoped to this file only."
`;
